-## 4. Flash
+`CONFIG_MODVERSIONS` is off, and a module's vermagic does not record the
+kernel config, so a module built against an older config still loads and can
+corrupt memory (turning on `CONFIG_IPV6`, for example, changes
+`struct net_device`). `build_kernel` does not rebuild the out-of-tree
+AIC8800 driver in `osdrv`, and older module copies stay in the Buildroot
+overlay and target, because nothing there deletes files.
+`build-rnsbox-kclean.sh` cleans and rebuilds the kernel and `osdrv`, checks
+that every shipped module carries the `5.10.4-rnsbox` vermagic, removes older
+module copies from the overlay and the Buildroot target, and packs an image.
+As with `build_all`, flash the image from the `build-rnsbox.sh` run that
+follows instead.
+
+`build-rnsbox.sh` catches the common cases: it warns when the built kernel
+lacks IPv6 (Reticulum's AutoInterface on `usb0` needs it), lacks the DS3231
+RTC driver, or predates RNSBox's `rtc-ds1307` fix; it rebuilds the AIC8800
+driver when that is older than the kernel config; it ships the kernel's
+installed modules and removes older copies from the overlay and target; and
+it stops when the kernel's installed modules are older than the kernel
+config.
+
+Buildroot does not notice a changed package recipe either. `build-rnsbox.sh`
+handles the packages listed above; for any other package you change, run
+`make -C buildroot <package>-dirclean` before packaging.
+
